summary:
@askalphaxiv for literature review is so good. they have embeddings for every paper and you can just query everything in natural language. much better than @elicitorg in my experience and certainly better than chatgpt/claude
i was looking into behavioral pessimism in LLMs today and alphaxiv served me some very interesting research on how model pessimism relates to safe completions and over-refusal
just a delightful experience with these guys

Most people won't read a 24-page paper. Most people will watch a 2-minute video about it.
@YahliHazan and I built post2vid at the @xai grokathon — a pipeline that turns any paper into an educational video.
To try it, Like this 👇
@post2vid explain

